.Dd November 17, 2026
.Dt CAL 1
.Os RavenBSD
.Sh NAME
.Nm cal
.Nd print a Gregorian calendar
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl 3 | Fl y
.Op Ar month Op Ar year
.Sh DESCRIPTION
The
.Nm
utility prints a calendar for the C locale.
With no operands it prints the
current month; with one operand it prints the whole year; with two operands
it prints the selected
.Ar month
and
.Ar year .
The
.Fl y
option selects the whole year (the current year when no operand is given),
and
.Fl 3
prints the previous, selected and next month side by side.
.Pp
The calendar is proleptic Gregorian: leap years are divisible by four, except
century years that are not divisible by four hundred.
The 1752 reform gap and
Julian dates are not modelled.
.Pp
Years are accepted from 1 through 9999.
A three-month view also needs the
neighbouring months, so its year must be between 2 and 9998.
With operands,
the month is 1 through 12 and the year includes the century.
.Pp
The protocol version 1 realtime clock returns zero, so the no-operand and
no-year views currently show January 1970 until a wall clock exists.
Explicit
.Ar month
and
.Ar year
operands do not depend on the clock.
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
A usage error exits with status 2. A clock or output failure exits with
status 1.
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr asa 1 ,
.Xr date 1
.Sh STANDARDS
RavenBSD implements the POSIX cal subset plus the
.Fl 3
and
.Fl y
views, with C-locale names only.
